     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Ravi held his hand in front of a torch and made a shadow on the wall.\n\"Light travels straight,\" said the teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "opaque",
     "transparent",
     "shadow"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Light travels in straight lines. An opaque object blocks light and makes a shadow. A transparent object lets light pass, and a translucent one lets some through.\nA shadow is bigger when the object is near the light and smaller when far away. Shadows change size and direction during the day.\nA pinhole camera makes an upside-down image on a screen because light rays cross at the small hole."
    }
